(version 1)

# Custom DRC rules for RejsaCAN v3.4.
#
# Board-setup constraints hold the JLCPCB 2-layer floors. These two rules cover
# what a flat global constraint cannot express.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Automotive spacing on the raw car supply.
#
# VCC is the 5-24V input straight off the vehicle. A 24V system's load dump
# (ISO 7637-2 pulse 5a) puts this net well above its nominal rail, so IPC-2221
# table 6-1 row B2 (external conductors, uncoated, <=3050m) asks for 0.6mm at
# 31-50V rather than the 0.1mm that applies at 0-30V.
#
# Scoped to tracks on purpose: the passives on this net are 0402/0603, whose own
# pad-to-pad gap is ~0.5mm and cannot be widened by a routing rule. Component
# choice sets the floor at the parts; routing is where the 0.6mm is winnable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "battery net track spacing (IPC-2221 B2, 31-50V)"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'Battery' && A.Type == 'Track'"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Documented exception: USB-C board-lock holes.
#
# The GT-USB-7010ASV puts its NPTH board locks 0.1944mm from the plated GND
# through-holes. That is the vendor's own geometry, and it is below JLCPCB's
# published hole-to-hole spacing -- but the fabricated v3.4 board carries it, so
# JLC evidently accepts it on this part.
#
# Narrowed to pairs inside USBC1 so the exception cannot silently excuse a real
# hole-spacing problem anywhere else on the board.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "USB-C vendor board-lock hole spacing (accepted exception)"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('USBC1') && B.memberOfFootprint('USBC1')"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Pad-to-pad spacing is set by the parts, not by the router.
#
# With the footprints corrected to the geometry actually fabricated, U2's real
# 2.045mm pads come within 0.189mm of C11 -- that is the board that was built and
# is working. JLCPCB's floor for SMD pads on different nets is 0.15mm, so it is
# manufacturable; it is only under the 0.2mm the net classes ask of *routing*.
#
# Scoped to pad-against-pad so tracks and vias keep the full net-class clearance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(rule "as-fabricated component pad spacing"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad'"))
